gner_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d06994209e205198b97b204c5546f5634735b45d73775813982ec772dd0b552f","event_uuid":"188085cf-035e-466b-81b4-af4c042cebe1","position":{"commit_sha":"1d226e99879d7c0247b8c4425c8c375e5c92c6f8","position":"1786076558104578001-188085cf-035e-466b-81b4-af4c042cebe1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"644afdff408e513620aea02bd2921db178b5ce9788d9620944c3fdd24805153c","event_uuid":"98b68a9b-5ffb-4e52-9e36-ef52fe94014d","position":{"commit_sha":"052bf8d4b7f7b9975e8da012612e9c0f787fd6bd","position":"1786086551824440001-98b68a9b-5ffb-4e52-9e36-ef52fe94014d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-223_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6ff494b3-b67f-4284-9d1e-818a0b7eecfd","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementer subagent finished (held-out: it never saw my validation). Investigation resolved the open question as (b): acli_cmd is purely an argv prefix for the ACLI binary (acli_subprocess.py:374-375, _DEFAULT_ACLI_CMD at :30), carries no target/credential, and every production construction site passes nothing; update_priority spawns no subprocess at all. So NO cross-target write exists -- signature hygiene, not a correctness bug. Param removed from update_priority + caller. String-grep for the name as a string: zero hits. Awaiting my held-out validation before commit.","timestamp":1786076558104578001}],"created_at":1786055577101728001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"62ee21b4-f300-4c4e-81c2-e9dabb08ca4b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b5a5-a93e-9013-4c37"}],"description":"`update_priority` (`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_cli_ops.py:417`) accepts a\nkeyword-only `acli_cmd: list[str] | None = None` and never reads it. The caller at\n`adapters/jira/acli.py:180` passes it **by keyword**:\n\n```python\nacli_cli_ops.update_priority(jira_key, priority_name, acli_cmd=acli_cmd)\n```\n\nThe sibling path in the same module does honour it — `_verify_created_issue(result.stdout,\nacli_cmd=acli_cmd, client=client)` at `:410`.\n\n## Be precise about what is and is not wrong\n\nThe function's docstring explains it deliberately bypasses ACLI:\n\n> ACLI does not support priority edit — uses direct REST API:\n> PUT /rest/api/3/issue/{key} with {\"fields\":{\"priority\":{\"name\":\"...\"}}}\n\nSo `acli_cmd` — an ACLI invocation vector — is **structurally inapplicable** to this function, not\nmerely unimplemented. The confirmed defect is therefore a signature that advertises a parameter it\ncannot use, with a caller passing it as though it matters. That is the same false-promise shape as\n`7504-a127-e9b0-42bb`.\n\n## The open question that decides severity\n\nInstead of using anything the caller supplied, the body resolves credentials ambiently:\n\n```python\n_s = acli_subprocess.resolve_jira_settings()\njira_url, user, api_token = _s.url, _s.user, _s.api_token\n```\n\n**If `acli_cmd` can encode a non-default Jira target** (a different site, instance, or credential\nset), then a deployment that configures one target would have priority updates go to the *ambient*\ntarget while every other write goes to the configured one — a cross-target write, which is a\ncorrectness bug rather than signature hygiene. **If `acli_cmd` only ever carries the ACLI binary\npath or invocation flags**, this reduces to removing a dead parameter.\n\nThis was NOT determined. Resolve it first; the remediation follows from the answer. Do not assume\nthe benign reading.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Determine whether `acli_cmd` can encode a Jira target distinct from what\n      `resolve_jira_settings()` returns; record the finding on this ticket with a citation\n- [x] If it can: priority updates resolve their target the same way the rest of the adapter does,\n      and a test pins that a non-default configured target is honoured\n- [x] If it cannot: `acli_cmd` is removed from `update_priority`'s signature and from the call site\n      at `acli.py:180`\n- [x] Either way, no function in this module accepts a parameter it cannot act on\n- [x] The docstring states how this REST path resolves credentials, since it differs from the\n      ACLI-based siblings around it","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","b5bc-f4f7-3433-4181"],["relates_to","b5a5-a93e-9013-4c37"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"b5bc-f4f7-3433-4181","parent_status_uuid":"a4227b87-7937-4ed9-a0fb-247676ad0566","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["janitor"],"ticket_id":"c9c6-a713-8bc6-4088","ticket_type":"bug","title":"update_priority accepts acli_cmd and cannot use it; credential resolution is ambient","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["6a30ce88-c967-4306-aed7-c56210a43c12","a4227b87-7937-4ed9-a0fb-247676ad0566","45987901-cf4a-4623-8d2a-a899abb69209","188085cf-035e-466b-81b4-af4c042cebe1","62ee21b4-f300-4c4e-81c2-e9dabb08ca4b","98b68a9b-5ffb-4e52-9e36-ef52fe94014d"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786086551824440002,"uuid":"33aa4173-8162-4035-a40d-a3acaafffcb6"}